Open gotohp-v1.3.0.exe after closing the old version. Use a small test folder. Keep Force Upload and Delete From Host off.
1. Record uploads
   Home → Upload Records → leave recording on. Upload two files using Upload Only. Confirm both appear in records afterward.
2. Skip recorded files
   Enable “Skip files recorded as uploaded.” Select those same files again. Expect 2 recorded, no transfer, and completion showing 2 locally recorded.
3. Mixed files
   Add one new file and select all three. Expect 2 recorded, 1 normal-upload candidate.
4. Album reuse
   Select the recorded files for a New album, then a Recent album. They should be added without retransferring. Check Google Photos to confirm.
5. Auto albums
   Select three folders with Auto Album. Confirm all three albums appear separately with correct counts.
6. Cancel
   Cancel during record checking—nothing should upload. Then cancel an upload after one file finishes; that completed file should remain recorded after restarting.
7. Records screen
   Test search, CSV export, and forgetting one record. Forgetting must not delete the actual file or Google Photos media.
8. Log button
   While a warning is visible, click the bottom-right log button. Repeat inside Settings and at compact/enlarged window sizes. It should remain visible and clickable.
If something fails, export the debug log and tell me the test number.
